      </div>

      <!-- PULL AND PINION STRATEGY -->
      <div class="eg-content-card" id="pull-strategy">
        <h2>Pull and Pinion Strategy</h2>
        <p>There are three types of pinions. Using the wrong one at the wrong time is one of the most common F2P mistakes.</p>
        <div class="pinion-table">
          <div class="pinion-row pinion-header">
            <div class="pinion-type">Type</div>
            <div class="pinion-pool">Pulls From</div>
            <div class="pinion-when">When To Use</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pinion-row">
            <div class="pinion-type">Normal Pinions</div>
            <div class="pinion-pool">All non-Starglint heroes</div>
            <div class="pinion-when">Anytime - the base pool</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pinion-row">
            <div class="pinion-type">Gold Pinions (faction)</div>
            <div class="pinion-pool">One specific faction</div>
            <div class="pinion-when">Only usable on faction rate-ups - the game does not allow them on the standard banner.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pinion-row">
            <div class="pinion-type">Rings (Starglint)</div>
            <div class="pinion-pool">Starglint heroes only</div>
            <div class="pinion-when">Rate-ups for Starglint heroes you already planned to build</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="eg-team-example">
          <h4>The Golden Rule</h4>
          <p><strong>Day 1-2:</strong> Spend freely to get a workable roster of 5 heroes.</p>
          <p><strong>Day 3 onward:</strong> Default to saving. Only pull on a rate-up when you can name the featured hero from memory. If you are pulling just because pulls are available, stop.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- DEITY SWAP EVENT -->
      <div class="eg-content-card" id="deity-swap">
        <h2>Deity Swap Event</h2>
        <p>The Deity Swap Event lets you transfer all investment from one hero - stats, awakening, everything - onto a different hero. It is one of the biggest safety nets for early mistakes.</p>
        <div class="eg-warning-box">
          <h3>Do Not Rush It</h3>
          <p>Wait until you have enough game knowledge to know which hero you want to swap into. Swapping into another bad pick wastes the event entirely.</p>
        </div>
        <h3>Good Swap Targets</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Swap out:</strong> heroes you built before reading a guide, old-meta carries that fell off, or duplicate roles you already have covered.</li>
          <li><strong>Swap into:</strong> your F2P core picks - Caishen, Yuelao, Hecate, Phoenix, or whichever carry is your team's current bottleneck.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Common Patterns</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Off a starter carry into a meta carry (e.g. early leveled hero into Hecate or Fengyi)</li>
          <li>Off an over-invested duplicate support into a tank</li>
          <li>Off a Starglint hero you no longer want to play</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- BEGINNER MISTAKES -->
      <div class="eg-content-card" id="mistakes">
        <h2>Common Beginner Mistakes</h2>
        <ul class="mistakes-list">
          <li><strong>Hoarding from Day 1.</strong> You need bodies on the field. Spend on Day 1-2, then switch to saving mode.</li>
          <li><strong>Spreading gear across six heroes.</strong> Your top two damage dealers get everything first. Supports do not need gear to fulfill their role.</li>
          <li><strong>Pulling on every banner.</strong> If you cannot name the featured hero, you are wasting pinions.</li>
          <li><strong>Chasing Zeus without the investment.</strong> Without Peerless rarity and Relic 30, he is an expensive average unit.</li>
          <li><strong>Using Poseidon below Relic 10.</strong> He underperforms at low relic levels. Build toward that breakpoint before relying on him.</li>
          <li><strong>Rushing Hecate before Relic 10.</strong> Her kit is incomplete below that level. She is a mid-to-late carry, not an early one.</li>
          <li><strong>Ignoring Shrine and Beacon Tree.</strong> These are the only investments that apply to every mode and every hero forever.</li>
          <li><strong>Burning the Deity Swap Event on impulse.</strong> Wait, think, then swap.</li>
          <li><strong>Building a second team before the first is finished.</strong> One team to Chapter 30, then diversify.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </main>
  </div>

